      }},
      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The oral administration to rats of the calcium antagonists nifedipine, nisoldipine and niludipine (3 mg/kg, 1-1.25 h before acute coronary ligation) greatly reduced the duration of ventricular tachycardia and fibrillation (VF) occurring in the first 30 min post-ligation period. The duration of VF was especially reduced (by 74-92%). None of the animals so treated died compared with a 40% mortality in the controls."},
